1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,540
This is the implementation demo for the platform gate.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:07,480
Unlike videos one to three, which walk through design mocks,

3
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:11,220
everything here is the real code running on this machine,

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:15,020
against a throwaway SQLite database with synthetic people.

5
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:20,140
It shows how a clean checkout becomes a working platform in about two minutes.

6
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:23,070
Start with the database.

7
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:28,590
Migration is an explicit command, and the API never applies it on startup.

8
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:34,690
The start script runs migrate, then seed, then launches the API and waits until it

9
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:35,740
reports ready.

10
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:39,830
Seed is safe to run again: the second run adds nothing.

11
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:43,860
And seed on a file that was never migrated is refused,

12
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:47,130
with a message telling you to migrate first.

13
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,650
Now the access rules.

14
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,130
The health endpoint is open to anyone.

15
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:57,290
Every other endpoint needs a token, so a request without one gets a four oh one

16
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:58,400
problem response.

17
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,470
We issue a local token for the synthetic buyer,

18
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:06,880
shown here with the secret part hidden, and the same request now succeeds and names

19
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:07,600
the caller.

20
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:12,430
That buyer token on an admin endpoint is turned away with a four oh three.

21
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:17,390
And when the server really does fail, the caller gets a five hundred problem

22
00:01:17,390 --> 00:01:20,850
response with a trace identifier, and no stack trace.

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,340
The buyer app starts and asks the real API whether it is ready.

24
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:31,570
An address that does not exist shows the four oh four page, with a way back.

25
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:34,120
Now we cut the connection to the API.

26
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:39,080
The app shows the five hundred page, with try again and contact support.

27
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:43,550
We restore the connection, press try again, and the app recovers.

28
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,540
Here is what to remember.

29
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:50,200
Migration and seeding are explicit and repeatable.

30
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:55,550
Endpoints require a valid token by default, and roles decide who gets in.

31
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:59,000
Failures are calm, structured, and recoverable.

32
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,250
Payments and video calls are local stand-ins in this gate,

33
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:05,890
and no real charge or email is made.

34
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:08,750
Next, journey one: sign up and sign in.
